# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Arca — environment
# Copy to `.env.local`. Every value here is optional: with none of them set the
# app boots against the in-memory fixture repository, which is how you develop
# the UI without a database. See backend/db/repository.ts.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# PostgreSQL. Set this and the app switches from fixtures to the real
# object-graph schema. Vercel Postgres and Neon both hand you this string.
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@host:5432/arca?sslmode=require"

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sign-in
#
# There is nothing to configure. Arca has no OAuth provider and no accounts:
# a member picks their name from the campaign roster and proves it with a PIN
# they choose on their first sign-in (backend/lib/pin.ts).
#
# Membership is NOT granted by signing in. A name appears on the roster only
# because it is a row in `campaign_members` for this campaign, which is the
# GM's decision and nobody else's. Adding someone is one statement:
#
#   INSERT INTO campaign_members (campaign_id, user_id, role)
#   VALUES ('<campaign id>', '<user id>', 'player');
#
# Resetting a forgotten PIN is one more — clearing the column puts that member
# back into the "choose a PIN" flow on their next sign-in:
#
#   UPDATE users SET pin_hash = NULL WHERE display_name = 'Kova';
#
# With fixtures (no DATABASE_URL) every member starts unenrolled and the
# roster resets whenever the dev server restarts, which is why `npm run dev`
# needs no database and no configuration at all.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The campaign this deployment serves. One campaign per deployment for now
# (SCOPE.md §13 Q5).
# ARCA_CAMPAIGN_ID="00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001"
